# APK build scaffolding (toolchain jars are ~50MB; fetch with android/fetch-tools.sh)
build/

# The release signing key IS committed, on purpose.
#
# android/release.keystore is a self-signed debug-grade key whose password is
# public in android/build.sh. It is not a secret: the game has no server, no
# accounts and no paid content, so the only thing this key does is give the app
# a stable *install identity*. If the key changed between releases, Android
# would refuse every upgrade with INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE -- which is
# far worse than the key being public. See docs/install-troubleshooting.md.
